{"text": "Melissa Fwu\n\nEXPERIENCE\nRepublican Party of Virginia July 2015 - Present\nSenior Deputy State Director Fairfax, Virginia\n\ne Oversaw the statewide activities of 43 field staff including training and development to maximize output\ntowards RNC election efforts in a top Presidential swing state\ne Directed top performing regions which consistently exceeded voter contact goals\ne Develop and implement statewide field strategy, goals, and messaging in coordination with State Director\ne Coordinated statewide outreach and engagement efforts in the Asian, Hispanic, and faith communities\n\nRepublican Party of Texas July 2013 \u2014 July 2015\nDirector of Asian American Engagement Austin, Texas\ne Developed and implemented a statewide political plan to increase Asian Pacific American (APA) Republican\nvoter turnout through identification of community partners, expanding Party\u2019s APA auxiliary to 300+ members,\nrecruiting volunteers, and organizing Republican presence at 80 community events\ne Party spokesperson to APA media sources, including television and radio interviews\ne Efforts resulted in Texas Republicans winning 53% (US Senator Cornyn) and 51% (Texas Governor Abbott) of the\nAsian vote in Texas\n\nThe European-Atlantic Group January 2011 \u2014 May 2011\nInternational Relations Intern London, UK\ne Organized, marketed, and executed high-profile debates featuring international political and diplomatic leaders\ne Developed marketing and fundraising strategies as a team to produce key event sponsorships\n\nUSA Pavilion \u2014 Shanghai World Exposition May 2010 \u2014 July 2010\nStudent Ambassador Shanghai, China\ne Showcased the United States and American innovation through presentations in Mandarin Chinese and English\nto media, key stakeholders, and over 20,000 international visitors a day\n\nOther: Texas House of Representatives, Legislative Aide (2013); Rice University Centennial Celebration, Student\nRelations Specialist; Sun Max Trading Company, Exec. Assistant (2009-2011); Littleton & Associates, Legal Intern (2011)\n\nEDUCATION\nRice University May 2012\nBachelor of Arts Double Major: Political Science and Policy Studies (GPA: 3.7) Houston, Texas\n\ne\u00a2 Concentration in International Relations; Law and Justice\ne Rice Global Urban Lab: Semester abroad in London and Istanbul; analyzed patterns of urban development in\nOlympic host cities and determine best practices for future bids\nLanguages: Fluent in Mandarin Chinese and Proficient in Spanish\n\nACTIVITIES\n\nBaker Institute for Public Policy \u2014 Student Forum 2009 - 2012\nEvents Chair (2011 \u2014 2012); Communications Director (2009-2011)\ne Lead Rice\u2019s largest political organization to promote student interest in politics and international relations\ne Directed campus-wide marketing and organizational efforts for up to 20 events a year featuring political and\ndiplomatic leaders from around the world\n\nRice University Honor Council 2009 - 2012\ne Elected University Representative\nBrown Residential College Committees 2009 - 2012\n\nSocials Coordinator; Brown Events Committee Chair; Senior Events Chair",
